WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.185
The Three Billy-Goats Gruff

00:00:02.885 --> 00:00:07.323
Once upon a time, there were three billy goats who lived down in a quiet valley.

00:00:07.673 --> 00:00:09.358
Their family name was Gruff.

00:00:09.708 --> 00:00:15.852
Across the valley, high upon a green mountain hillside, grew sweet clover and tender meadow grass.

00:00:16.202 --> 00:00:21.834
The three goats looked up from the valley and longed to climb the hillside to feast and grow fat.

00:00:22.484 --> 00:00:28.863
To reach that sunny hillside, they had to cross a rushing mountain stream that tumbled over rocks and stones.

00:00:29.213 --> 00:00:34.269
And right across the water stretched a narrow wooden bridge made of heavy timber planks.

00:00:34.919 --> 00:00:45.863
Now, under that very bridge lived a great, ugly troll! He had eyes as round and big as saucers, a long crooked nose like a poker, and messy moss in his hair.

00:00:46.213 --> 00:00:50.522
He was always grumpy, and he guarded his bridge so that no one could pass.

00:00:51.172 --> 00:00:55.524
Early the next morning, the smallest Billy Goat Gruff set off down the path.

00:00:55.874 --> 00:00:59.799
He had tiny hooves, soft cream-colored fur, and little button horns.

00:01:00.149 --> 00:01:04.757
Even though he was the littlest, he trotted along with a brave and cheerful heart.

00:01:05.407 --> 00:01:07.562
He stepped right onto the wooden bridge.

00:01:07.912 --> 00:01:10.643
His tiny hooves tapped lightly against the boards.

00:01:10.993 --> 00:01:14.406
Trip, trap, trip, trap! went the bridge under his little feet.

00:01:15.056 --> 00:01:24.080
Suddenly, a terrible roar boomed from beneath the timber planks! The ugly troll poked his head over the rail, his saucer eyes wide with anger.

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:27.289
Who's that tripping over my bridge? roared the troll.

00:01:27.939 --> 00:01:34.040
Oh, it is only I, the tiniest Billy Goat Gruff, said the little goat in his small, squeaky voice.

00:01:34.390 --> 00:01:37.505
I am going up to the hillside to make myself fat.

00:01:37.855 --> 00:01:40.969
Now I am coming to gobble you up! shouted the troll.

00:01:41.319 --> 00:01:45.181
Oh, please don't take me! I am far too little, said the clever goat.

00:01:45.531 --> 00:01:48.197
Wait a moment for the second Billy Goat Gruff.

00:01:48.547 --> 00:01:54.713
He is much bigger than I am! Well, be off with you then! grunted the greedy troll, thinking of a bigger meal.

00:01:55.063 --> 00:01:58.049
And the smallest goat skipped safely across to the meadow.

00:01:58.699 --> 00:02:02.113
A little while later, down came the second Billy Goat Gruff.

00:02:02.463 --> 00:02:07.135
He was medium-sized, with a warm brown coat, sturdy legs, and curved horns.

00:02:07.485 --> 00:02:10.983
He trotted down toward the stream, eager to join his brother.

00:02:11.633 --> 00:02:13.809
The second goat trotted onto the bridge.

00:02:14.159 --> 00:02:17.018
His hooves made a firmer, louder click on the wood.

00:02:17.368 --> 00:02:21.741
Trip, trap, trip, trap, trip, trap! went the bridge under his steady stride.

00:02:22.391 --> 00:02:27.575
Up popped the troll's hairy head once more! Who's that tripping over my bridge? roared the troll.

00:02:27.925 --> 00:02:32.533
It is I, the second Billy Goat Gruff, said the goat in a clear, bold voice.

00:02:32.883 --> 00:02:35.998
I am going up to the hillside to make myself fat.

00:02:36.348 --> 00:02:39.335
Now I am coming to gobble you up! howled the troll.

00:02:39.685 --> 00:02:42.991
Oh no, do not take me! said the second goat calmly.

00:02:43.341 --> 00:02:45.859
Wait a little while for Big Billy Goat Gruff.

00:02:46.209 --> 00:02:51.201
He is much, much bigger than I! Very well! Be off with you! growled the greedy troll.

00:02:51.551 --> 00:02:55.391
And the second goat bounded safely across to the grassy hillside.

00:02:56.041 --> 00:02:59.027
Just then, a deep shadow fell across the forest path.

00:02:59.377 --> 00:03:11.196
Down came the great, magnificent Big Billy Goat Gruff! He was enormous and strong, with thick shaggy grey fur, a long wispy beard, and two great curved horns as hard as stone.

00:03:11.546 --> 00:03:24.154
He strode onto the bridge, and the heavy timbers creaked and groaned under his mighty weight: TRIP, TRAP, TRIP, TRAP, TRIP, TRAP! Who's that tramping over my bridge? roared the troll, leaping up onto the boards.

00:03:24.504 --> 00:03:30.392
IT IS I! THE BIG BILLY GOAT GRUFF! boomed the giant goat in a voice like rolling thunder.

00:03:30.742 --> 00:03:33.643
Now I am coming to gobble you up! cried the troll.

00:03:33.993 --> 00:03:37.065
Well, come along then! shouted Big Billy Goat Gruff.

00:03:37.415 --> 00:03:53.799
He lowered his mighty horns, charged right at the bully, and with a tremendous crack and a great heave, butted the troll right off the bridge and down into the rushing river! Splash! Away the soggy troll tumbled down the cascade, never to bother anyone again!

00:03:54.449 --> 00:03:59.911
Then Big Billy Goat Gruff strode triumphantly across the bridge to join his two brothers.

00:04:00.261 --> 00:04:07.130
Up on the sunny hillside, the three Billy Goats Gruff ate the sweet green clover and tender grass all summer long.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:19.171
They grew so fat and round they could scarcely walk home again! And if the fat hasn't fallen off them, why, they are still fat to this very day! Snip, snap, snout, this tale's told out!
